<h1> Passions </h1>

<h2> Disability Adovacy</h2>

<p> I have been doing disability advocacy since I was 11 years old. The passion came from not being heard as a child. As someone with ADHD and Cerebral Palsy, I did not really feel heard. Not heard in education, law-making, or societal aspects. I know it is the same for others in the disabled community. I use my design skills to create artistic pieces related to disability issues. You can check them out at</p> 

<a href="https://chrissysgallery.myportfolio.com">ChrissysGallery</a>

 <p> My goal is to help as many people possible especially children through education, adovacy, and support. I learned about the ramifications of what happens when disabled people are left behind so I want to do my part. </p>
 

<h2> Children's Media</h2>
<p> Children are key to changing the world. I mean, a perfect example is myself. Though sometimes it was tough , my experiences prepared me to be the advocate I am today. I want children to learn more about disabled people because when I looked back at my own experiences, it incorrect beliefs that led to my bullying. I believe that the next generation ( with guidance ) can be wonderful and  well rounded human beings. My hope is that with my art that I am able to mold the next genration to help them be good people. I believe that media holds the key as I learned so much, and it is the first time a child sees who they can be a and the world around them.
</p>

